# Authorization and capabilities

Read the backend contracts linked from `docs/PROJECT_FACTS.md` and inspect the current action's permission checks.

- `packages/web/src/shared/lib/roles.ts` describes numeric Zulip roles. It is not a Workspace authorization model.
- Workspace IAM capability loading is in `packages/web/src/entities/workspace-auth/workspace-iam-capabilities.model.ts`. Use the relevant server-derived resource/action capability and current scope.
- Keep loading, unsupported, denied, and allowed states distinct. Do not infer permission from a display role/name or fabricate capabilities.
- UI visibility is not server authorization; handle backend denial for actions even when the control was enabled.
- Capability responses are owner-scoped asynchronous data; stale responses must not grant access in a different organization/project.
